.TH tkutlclip n 0.1 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkutlclip
.PP
Copy \fBtablelist\fR rows to the clipboard as TSV or CSV — the common "Ctrl+C copies the selection as spreadsheet\-pasteable text" behaviour that tablelist itself does not provide. Library\-neutral.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tkutils::tkutlclip 0.1
.CE
.PP
Requires \fBTk\fR and \fBtablelist\fR. Uses \fBtclutils::tucsv\fR for CSV quoting when available (falls back to a built\-in quoter otherwise).
.SS Commands
.CS
::tkutils::tkutlclip::copySelection   tbl ?options?
::tkutils::tkutlclip::copyAll         tbl ?options?
::tkutils::tkutlclip::asText          tbl rows ?options?
::tkutils::tkutlclip::installBindings tbl ?options?
.CE
.PP
\fBtbl\fR is the tablelist widget. \fBcopySelection\fR/\fBcopyAll\fR return the number of rows copied; \fBasText\fR returns the built string without touching the clipboard.
.SS Options
.TS
l l l.
Option	Default	Meaning
\fB\-format\fR	\fBtsv\fR	\fBtsv\fR or \fBcsv\fR
\fB\-header\fR	\fB0\fR	prepend column titles as the first line
\fB\-formatted\fR	\fB1\fR	use displayed values (\fBgetformatted\fR) vs raw cells
\fB\-columns\fR	\fBvisible\fR	\fBvisible\fR (skip hidden columns) or \fBall\fR
.TE
.SS Usage
.CS
package require Tk
package require tablelist
package require tkutils::tkutlclip

tablelist::tablelist .t -columns {0 Article left 0 Qty right 0 Price right}
# ... insert rows ...

# Ctrl+C copies the selected rows as TSV
::tkutils::tkutlclip::installBindings .t

# Copy everything as CSV with a header row
::tkutils::tkutlclip::copyAll .t -format csv -header 1
.CE
.PP
Get the text without using the clipboard:
.CS
set tsv [::tkutils::tkutlclip::asText .t {0 1 2} -header 1]
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
TSV replaces embedded tabs/newlines with spaces so pasted cells stay aligned. Use CSV when cells may contain those characters and you need them preserved.
.IP \(bu
\fBinstallBindings\fR binds \fB<<Copy>>\fR on the tablelist body, so it coexists with normal text\-entry copy in edited cells.
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TKUTILS TKUTLCLIP <REASON>}\fR (\fBOPTION\fR, \fBFORMAT\fR, \fBCOLUMNS\fR).
